<main>
  <h1>MediCare Connect – Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>

  <p>MediCare Connect ("the app") helps patients in rural South African communities keep track of their
  medication, and helps Community Health Workers (CHWs) manage medication deliveries. This policy explains
  what personal information the app collects, why, who it is shared with, and the choices you have. We
  handle personal information in line with South Africa's Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA).</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The app is developed by the MediCare Connect project team (PROG7314 Group 5). For any privacy question,
  contact us at <strong>kimkganyago@gmail.com ,wavhudibudeli96@gmail.com,tshegofatjotau@gmail.com ,karabokaari@gmail.com</strong>. You may also complain to
    tshegofatjotau@gmail.com </strong>.</p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Information</th><th>Why we need it</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Email address and password (stored by Firebase Authentication), or your Google account sign-in details</td><td>To create your account and sign you in.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Full name, date of birth, ID or clinic number, phone number, village or location</td><td>To identify the patient and let the clinic and CHWs reach them.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Account type (Patient or Caregiver) and an optional caregiver or guardian phone number</td><td>To show the right view and let a family member or caregiver be contacted.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Medication details, dose confirmations ("I took it"), supply counts and alerts</td><td>To track adherence and warn when supply is running low.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Delivery records (patient name, address, status, proof of delivery such as a PIN or name)</td><td>To let CHWs schedule and confirm medication deliveries.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>A push-notification token for your device</td><td>To send you reminders and alerts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Language, high-contrast and font-size settings</td><td>To remember your accessibility choices on your device.</td></tr>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>Health-related information (your medication and dose history) is sensitive. We collect only what the
  app needs to work.</p>

  <h2>3. Biometric unlock</h2>
  <p>If you turn on fingerprint or face unlock, the check is done by your phone's operating system. The app
  never receives, stores or sends your fingerprint or face data.</p>

  <h2>4. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the app's features: medication tracking, early supply alerts, deliveries and emergency contact.</li>
    <li>To keep your data available if your connection drops, and to sync it when you are back online.</li>
    <li>To send notifications you have allowed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your information and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Your information is processed by service providers that run the app. They act on our behalf and do not
  use it for their own purposes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Authentication, Realtime Database and Cloud Messaging) – stores your account and app data and delivers notifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Sign-In</strong> – only if you choose to sign in with Google.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosted REST API</strong> (hosted on Render) – receives delivery records so CHWs and clinics can see them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your data may therefore be processed on servers outside South Africa. We may also disclose information
  if the law requires it.</p>

  <h2>6. Security</h2>
  <p>Data is sent over encrypted connections (HTTPS). Database rules allow each signed-in user to read and
  write only their own data. Your data is excluded from device cloud backups. No system is completely secure,
  so please keep your device and password safe.</p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep your information while your account is active. When you ask us to delete your account, we
  delete your personal data, except where the law requires us to keep it.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under POPIA you may ask to see, correct or delete your personal information, object to its processing,
  or withdraw your consent. To do any of these, email <strong>kimkganyago@gmail.com ,wavhudibudeli96@gmail.com,karabokaari@gmail.com, tshegofatjotau@gmail.com ,]</strong>. You may also complain to
    tshegofatjotau@gmail.com </strong>. You may also complain to
  South Africa's Information Regulator (<a href="https://inforegulator.org.za">inforegulator.org.za</a>).</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>The app is intended for adult patients and their caregivers or guardians. A parent or guardian may
  manage the account of a person in their care.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this page. Significant changes will also
  be shown in the app.</p>
</main>
</body>
